.TH RUMB 1 "2026-11-02" "rumb 0.1.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rumb \- terminal dashboard for the health of a NixOS system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rumb
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-anim ]
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-\-offline ]
.br
.B rumb\-scan \-\-stream
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-\-offline ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rumb
is a terminal dashboard for NixOS.
It shows the flake inputs that are behind their remotes, ranked by risk;
the crashes, failed units, journal errors and niri config errors since the
current system generation was built;
the system generations kept for a rollback;
the space left on
.IR /nix " and " /boot ;
whether the running kernel differs from the one the current generation boots;
the programs that still run files of an older generation;
and the NixOS announcements published since the last switch.
.PP
rumb only reads.
It never builds, switches, updates the flake lock or collects garbage,
and it never asks for root.
The commands it names, such as
.B nix flake update
or
.BR "nixos\-rebuild switch \-\-rollback" ,
are hints to run yourself.
.PP
After the scan rumb keeps following the journal and the system profile:
a switch to a new generation shows as a live event and starts a new scan.
.SH LAYOUT
rumb starts with the instruments and the eye with the subsystems;
keys 3, 4 and 5 add the lists of updates, problems and live events.
The default layout fits a terminal of 120 columns and 34 rows,
and every panel together fits 150 columns and 47 rows.
A smaller terminal hides the eye with the subsystems first,
then the lists that do not fit side by side,
then the instruments, whose checks then show on one line under the header.
When none of the chosen panels fits, the updates and problems lists stand in.
Hidden panels show their key in yellow.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Play bundled demo data instead of checking this system.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-anim
Show the results without animation.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colors to use.
By default rumb uses the theme chosen with
.BR esc ,
else
.BR shadesofjade .
.B system
follows the current Noctalia colors live as they change.
.TP
.B \-\-themes
List the theme names.
.TP
.BI \-\-since " time"
Look for problems since
.IR time ,
for example
.BR "7 days ago" .
The default is when the current system generation was created.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Do not ask the flake input remotes and do not fetch the NixOS news.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B 1\(en5
Show or hide the instruments, the subsystems with the eye, the updates, the problems and the live events.
When the updates panel is large enough, 3 switches it between the map, the rows and hidden.
.TP
.BR tab ", " shift+tab
Move the focus to the next or previous of the instruments, the subsystems and the lists.
.TP
.BR left ", " right
Select an instrument or a part of the subsystems.
.TP
.BR up ", " down ", " PgUp ", " PgDn ", " Home ", " End
Select a row of the focused list.
.TP
.B enter
Open the selected row, instrument or part.
.TP
.BR / ", " f
Filter the focused list.
.TP
.B j
Show the journal of the selected problem.
.TP
.B c
Copy the text of the open window.
.TP
.B e
Export a Markdown report to
.IR ~/rumb\-exports .
.TP
.B esc
Close or clear.
With nothing open, show the options in the eye, where
.BR left " and " right
change the theme and typing filters the themes.
.TP
.B r
Scan again.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH RUMB\-SCAN
.B rumb\-scan \-\-stream
runs the checks and prints one JSON event per line,
then keeps following the journal and the system profile.
It reads
.IR /nix/var/nix/profiles ,
.IR /run/current\-system ,
.IR /run/booted\-system ,
the flake lock, the journal, the core dumps and
.IR /proc .
The flake inputs are compared with
.B git ls\-remote
when git is installed, else through the git smart HTTP endpoint with
.BR curl .
The NixOS news needs
.BR xmllint .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUMB_FLAKE
Directory of the system flake whose
.I flake.lock
is checked (default
.IR /etc/nixos ).
.TP
.B RUMB_THEME
Theme to use when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B RUMB_SCAN
Path of the
.B rumb\-scan
to run.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, or without a terminal, print the Markdown report of one scan.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rumb/theme
The theme chosen in the options
.RI ( $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rumb/theme
when that is set).
.TP
.I ~/.config/noctalia/colors.json
The current Noctalia colors, used by the
.B system
theme.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nix3\-store\-diff\-closures (1),
.BR nixos\-rebuild (8),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR coredumpctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
